The smoking gun would be CDN cache hit/miss metrics on the manifest endpoint: if the cache policy excludes session/targeting parameters and the hit ratio is very high, that confirms most viewers get identical cached responses. Cross-referencing CDN viewer-request volume against MediaTailor's own origin-request count should also show a huge gap — thousands of viewers but only a handful actually reaching MediaTailor — which proves nearly everyone is served a stale, shared manifest instead of a freshly personalized one.

